      "after": "Ordinary calls have a fixed limit. Each successfully opened descriptor reserves exactly one TERM, KILL and close record. Reserved calls require the opened descriptor, exact allowed argument shape and unused per-descriptor operation. New opens and signal-zero calls still refuse at the ordinary limit. Failed-open validation also uses its reserved close.",
      "before": "One global call count could consume the last record in pidfd_open and reject the required close."
